      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The state of the lymphatic heart perfusion has been studied experimentally on dogs with intact myocardium (control 1), with acute myocardial ischemia (AMI) model (control 2) and during injection of heparin, rheogluman and obsidan in AMI. It has been stated that AMI induces acute distress of the lymphatic heart perfusion system occurring at the first minutes after the onset of the focal myocardial ischemia. Heparin, rheogluman and obsidan demonstrated selective stimulating effect on the function of the lymphatic myocardial system."},
